From 01de0846fd911cc86f9432ee2b67c9402c8ffe18 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artur Szafraniec <ganggg111@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 12:51:23 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 13/40] ufs: exynos: report the state of the protector, and
 leave it alone

The fourth window of this controller is not only a hardware encryption
unit. The same block holds the unit that decides what of memory the
controller may reach, and with it shut the link comes up and then every
transfer request times out, because the controller cannot fetch the request
from memory.

So the window is taken and the state of the region descriptors is printed,
and nothing is written to them.  Reading them is enough to say whether the
boot loader may use storage at all, and writing them is firmware's
business: on this SoC the descriptors answer to EL3 and a write from here
takes the whole system down with an external abort.

The window that says whether the host snoops caches is taken here too.
Those bits are cleared, because the boot loader maps everything uncached: a
host that writes its completion status coherently has that write thrown
away by the invalidate that follows.

Signed-off-by: Artur Szafraniec <ganggg111@gmail.com>
---
 .../arm/dts/exynos9820-beyond2lte-u-boot.dtsi |  30 +-
 drivers/ufs/ufs-exynos.c                      | 307 +++++++++++++++---
 drivers/ufs/ufs-exynos.h                      |  19 ++
 3 files changed, 295 insertions(+), 61 deletions(-)

